# matching static asset exists, so /* must not rewrite robots.txt, sitemap.xml,
# or llms.txt (those would otherwise fall through to the SPA HTML shell).
/robots.txt /robots.txt 200
/sitemap.xml /sitemap.xml 200
/llms.txt /llms.txt 200
/34af1a9e03fae2647e2d32b44b8a08a5.txt /34af1a9e03fae2647e2d32b44b8a08a5.txt 200

# www → apex cannot be done here. Cloudflare Pages _redirects does not
# support domain-level / host redirects (source must be a path). Do not
# add `/* https://thepubliccap.com/:splat 301` — that would 301 the apex.
# Do not add functions/_middleware.js for this: a root middleware invokes
# Functions on every request and Pages then ignores this file (coach-fa
# splat + crawl identity proxies would have to be rewritten in JS).
# Dashboard + DNS (outside this repo) — official Pages www guide:
#   1. Proxied A www → 192.0.2.1 (or attach www as a Pages custom domain).
#   2. Bulk Redirect: www.thepubliccap.com → https://thepubliccap.com
#      301, preserve query string, subpath matching, preserve path suffix.
# Today www.thepubliccap.com has no DNS record.

# Do not 200-rewrite exact SPA paths — or /school/:id — to /index.html.
# html_handling pretty-URLs /index.html → / with a 308, and a rewrite
# would also serve homepage title/canonical to crawlers. Exact shells
# and school/{id}.html come from scripts/write-spa-html.mjs.
# Old buyout share links. Static /buyout/<id>.html shells are the canonical
# pages — do not 200-rewrite /buyout/* to /index.html (that would hide them).
# Do not add `/buyout?school=:school /buyout/:school 301`. Cloudflare Pages
# ignores query strings when matching a redirect source, so that rule matches
# bare `/buyout` and 301s it to the literal path `/buyout/:school` (the
# placeholder is never filled). `/buyout` is buyout.html, the calculator.
# `/buyout?school=<id>` stays on that shell; Buyout.jsx replace-navigates to
# `/buyout/<id>`. No rule may emit `/buyout/:school`.

# Keep /coach-fa/* for detail URLs that are not prerendered files.
/coach-fa/* /index.html 200
